<!-- @after Common Pitfalls :: check -->
**Review the dependency.** Decide before opening each answer.

<details><summary><code>:feature:search:impl</code> adds <code>implementation(project(":feature:product:impl"))</code> to open a product screen.</summary>

Reject it. Depend on `:feature:product:api` and navigate with the product route defined there; the app's graph supplies the implementation.
</details>

<details><summary>A new <code>DateFormats.kt</code> helper goes into <code>:core:common</code>, used by one feature.</summary>

Keep it in that feature. A core module changed for one consumer still reaches every module downstream of it.
</details>

<details><summary><code>:feature:cart:api</code> declares <code>fun interface CartNavigator { fun open(activity: Activity) }</code>.</summary>

It pulls Android into an API module that could be pure Kotlin. Pass a route or a callback type instead, so consumers' unit tests do not need an Android runtime.
</details>
